  "worked_solution": "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,3\\,)}_{\u23df}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,7\\,)}_{\u23df}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]= \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
